---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Action from '../components/Action.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy information | AVA at Palm Jumeirah" description="How information submitted through this website's enquiry form is used and how to make a privacy request.">
 <div class="inner-page site-width">
  <div class="inner-header"><Header/></div>
  <main id="main" class="legal">
   <a class="text-link" href="/">← Back to AVA</a>
   <h1 class="display">Privacy information</h1>
   <p>This page describes the enquiry service on this website. It applies to information you choose to submit through its forms.</p>
   <h2>Information you provide</h2>
   <p>The enquiry form asks for your name and email address, an optional phone number, and your permission to be contacted. It also includes the residence or feature you selected, so your request has the right context. A privacy request may include a message.</p>
   <h2>How your enquiry is used</h2>
   <p>Your submission is stored in a private enquiry inbox managed by the owner of this website. It is used to review and respond to your request. This form does not automatically forward your information to a developer, property operator, or external sales team.</p>
   <p>The website uses Vercel for hosting and private form storage. These services process the information needed to run the website and receive your enquiry.</p>
   <h2>Form security</h2>
   <p>The form includes validation and measures to reduce automated submissions. A submission identifier allows a retried request to be recognised without creating another enquiry. If a request cannot be saved, the form shows an error and keeps your entered details available for another attempt.</p>
   <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
   <p>This website does not add advertising or analytics cookies. The interactive gallery, menus and floor-plan viewer run in your browser without an account.</p>
   <h2>Your choices</h2>
   <p>You can browse the website without submitting an enquiry. To ask about information you have submitted, or request access, correction or deletion, send a privacy request using the same email address. Include enough detail to identify the enquiry; do not include sensitive documents.</p>
   <div class="privacy-action"><Action label="Make a privacy request" action="enquire" context="Privacy request" caption="Your information"/></div>
  </main>
 </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.legal>.text-link{font-size:14px;margin-bottom:32px}.privacy-action{margin-top:32px}</style>
